{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>His father wept for him.</b> Our predecessors expounded it of Isaac. And in truth Isaac did not die until Joseph was twenty-nine years old. Some say that prophecy departed from both of them because of their mourning, and their testimony is the matter of Elisha:" "<b>And all his daughters.</b> His daughter and his son's daughter," "And the word שאולה, like מטה, and the meaning is the grave. And here the translator erred for those who stray, for he translated שאולה as Gehenna. But behold: כי לא שאול תודך (Isaiah 38:18), ואציעה שאול הנך (Psalms 139:8) — the opposite of אם אסק שמים שם אתה (ibid.), ערום שאול נגדו (Job 26:6), and many others:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "The closing reference to Elisha is obscure; rendered literally. The allusion is to 2 Kings 3 where Elisha prophesies in the context of a bereaved father."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:22.197081307Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}